<title>TURKMENISTAN: Turkmen H1 natgas output crashes 46 percent.</title>
<headline>Turkmen H1 natgas output crashes 46 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ASHGABAT 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkmenistan's production of natural gas fell to 12.15 billion cubic metres, or bcm, in the first half of this year, a 46 percent drop year-on-year, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p> TURKMEN ENERGY OUTPUT	 June 97     May 97    Jan-June 97</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p> (billion cubic metres)	 0.551	0.617	12.151</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	  -10.7	-30.4	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 -46.0</p>
<p> Crude oil (tonnes)	   384,000    360,500   2,041,700</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   +6.5	 +8.4	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	  +4.7</p>
<p> Gasoline (tonnes)	     52,500     64,500     279,300</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	  -18.6	+53.9	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 -31.7</p>
<p> Diesel (tonnes)		324,100    137,000     854,000</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	 +136.6	+53.6	   n/a</p>
<p>  yr/yr   pct change	    n/a	  n/a	 +11.1</p>
<p> Fuel oil (mazut) (tonnes)  118.500    115.100     810.900</p>
<p>  mth/mth pct change	   +3.0	-17.2	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr  pct change	    n/a	  n/a	  +4.1</p>
<p>The committee said a sharp fall in natural gas output in the first half of the year was largely due to the suspension of gas exports in March.</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
